  "abilities": [],
  "behavior": "It is aggressive and uses claw-and-tail combos. It can also burrow to surprise its target with an attack from below. It is commonly found near Northern Scorpion eggs or alongside scorplings, so it is rarely safe to assume it is completely alone.",
  "interactionWithPlayer": "It is much less durable than an adult but still has attacks capable of dealing heavy damage. It can be especially dangerous if the player underestimates it because of its size or loses track of where it burrowed.",
  "interactionWithCreatures": "It often stays near Northern Scorpion eggs and scorplings, while also sharing territory with other members of its species. It may also become involved in fights with other creatures entering the area.",
  "strategy": "Use Busting damage and take advantage of its lower health to kill it quickly. Check the surroundings before starting the fight because scorplings or other scorpions may be nearby. If it begins to burrow, prepare to dodge or block the attack as it emerges.",
